1,Music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Australia,"Music of Australia The music of Australia has an extensive history made of music societies. Indigenous Australian music forms a significant part of the unique heritage of a 40,000- to 60,000-year history which produced the iconic didgeridoo.",Mariyedi,Australian
2,"Mariyedi Language (ZMY) - L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/zmy/,"Mariyedi is an endangered indigenous language of Australia. It belongs to the Australian language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by the elderly only. It is not known to be taught in schools.",Mariyedi,Australian
